# D-105 native, the result route (steps/d105-native.md §5): `mk () Model`
# returns `o: Other`: its `return:` records o in the arena's implements table with the pair Other -> Model
# (its result is marked), and `rd(mk())` passes the call's result on -- the site picks the pair by the
# value's record: m\a = 10.  Before: 20 (and, until D-108, gcc refused the caller).  Success is 7.
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
    size_t: b 2U
end: Model
Other:
    size_t: b 20U
    size_t: a 10U
end: Other
fn: rd (Model: m) size_t
return: m\a
fn: mk () Model
    Other: o
    return: o
fn: go () size_t
    return: rd(mk())
size_t: got 0U
got: go()
int: ok 3
if: got = 10U
    ok: 7
if: got = 20U
    ok: 5
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
